": " ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Listen to each audio. Select the objects that belong to Tony and Jane in the table.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You have 2 attempts to submit your answers.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}]}], "type": "TAB", "template_override": 1}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Places and People", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": " Is There a Dictionary?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "Beginner", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pencil ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an object we use for writing or drawing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Can I use your pencil? I  want  to write a note. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le03ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a classroom.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "eraser ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small object we use to remove pencil marks", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:    Do you have an eraser? I need to change something.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le03ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dictionary", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a book that has the meaning of words in a language ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Can I use your dictionary? I don't know how to spell a word.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le03ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ruler", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a classroom object we use to measure and draw lines", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I need a ruler to draw something. Do you have one?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le03ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "desk ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a table we use to  write or work ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are three pencils on the desk.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le03ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "big", "type": "name"}, {"content": "large in size ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My desk is big. I have all my pencils and my dictionary on it!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le03ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "small", "type": "name"}, {"content": "limited in size", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My desk is small. I have no space for writing!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le03ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Asking and Saying Where Things Are", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">there is</span> or <span class=\"strong\">there are</span> to say that something is in a specific place. <br /> You use <span class=\"strong\">is there</span> or <span class=\"strong\">are there</span> to ask about something. <br />You use <span class=\"strong\">where is</span> or <span class=\"strong\">where are</span> to ask where something is.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":\"4\",\"columns\":\"3\",\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Singular\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Plural\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Statements with <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> There</ span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"There is <br/>There's  <br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Example: There's a pencil on the desk.</ span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"There are <br/> <br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Example: There are many pencils on the desk.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Questions with <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> There</ span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Is there \u2026 ? <br/><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Example: Is there a pencil on the desk?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Are there \u2026 ? <br/><br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Example: Are there any pencils on the desk?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Questions with <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Where</ span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Where is \u2026 ? <br/>Where's \u2026 ? <br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Example: Where's the pencil?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Where are \u2026 ?  <br/><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Example: Where are the pencils?</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"prelo-letter-page-break\">", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Describing Objects", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\"> adjectives</span> to describe objects. <br />You put adjectives before the noun or after the verb <span class=\"strong\"> to be</span>. <br/> These are the most common types of adjectives: color, size, quality and age.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There is a <span class=\"strong\">red</span> pencil on the desk. (before the noun) ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The pencil is <span class=\"strong\">small</span>. (after the verb)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":\"05\",\"columns\":\"02\",\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Types of Adjectives</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Examples </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"color\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> red, blue, green, yellow </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"size\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> big, small, short, long</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"quality\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">good, bad, nice </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"age\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> old, new</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "There are <span class=\"strong\">good</span> books in the classroom. (before the noun)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The books are <span class=\"strong\">new</span>. (after the verb)", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Use information about locations of things to interact with others.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands basic information in English texts according to the communicative topics of this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands basic information in English texts according to the communicative topics of this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Uses an appropriate range of basic vocabulary and structures to describe location of classroom objects. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands basic information in English texts according to the communicative topics of this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Uses an appropriate range of basic vocabulary and structures to describe location of classroom objects. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Uses an appropriate range of basic vocabulary and structures to describe location of classroom objects. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Uses an appropriate range of basic vocabulary and structures to describe location of classroom objects. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands basic information in English texts according to the communicative topics of this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn1le03ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go on the Internet. Find pictures of classrooms in different countries. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find a classroom in North America, Africa and Asia. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What do you see? Make a list of the objects. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare the different classrooms with your classroom. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about the differences with your partner. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about things in a classroom. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use expressions to say where things are. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe 3 different classrooms. ", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}